secubox-health-doctor (1.0.2-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * L'unite retire sa socket perimee via `ExecStartPre=+/bin/rm`.
    /run/secubox porte le bit collant : on n'y delie que ce qu'on possede,
    et une socket laissee par un autre utilisateur rend le demarrage
    impossible — le service echoue, redemarre, echoue encore, en silence.
  * `RuntimeDirectory=secubox` retire : systemd efface le contenu d'un
    RuntimeDirectory au redemarrage, et ce repertoire est partage par ~95
    unites. Une seule qui le declare emporte les sockets des autres.

 -- Gerald KERMA <devel@cybermind.fr>  Sun, 16 Aug 2026 10:35:59 +0200

secubox-health-doctor (1.0.1-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Drop act-runner-arm64 from vital REGISTRY (#214). A stopped CI runner
    doesn't break the board and shouldn't count as a vital-service failure.
    The check_act_runner_arm64 function is kept at module level for reuse
    by a future REGISTRY_INFORMATIONAL tier.

 -- Gerald KERMA <devel@cybermind.fr>  Tue, 19 May 2026 07:53:56 +0200

secubox-health-doctor (1.0.0-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Initial release (issue #212).
  * Daemon + healthctl CLI + FastAPI exposing /api/v1/health-doctor/.
  * 11 vital-service checks: haproxy, nginx, secubox-metrics, secubox-hub,
    mitmproxy LXC, gitea LXC, mail LXC + ports 25/465/587/993, cookie-audit
    ledger mtime, crowdsec + lapi, filesystems mounted RW, optional
    act-runner-arm64 LXC.
  * Eighth verb of the SecuBox grammar — closes the ops-monitoring layer
    parallel to haproxyctl/giteactl/mitmproxyctl/dropletctl/etc.
  * Persisted state cache at /var/cache/secubox/health-doctor.json.
  * State transitions (ok->fail, fail->ok) emit structured journal events
    for CSPN compliance.
  * 60s timer + on-demand `healthctl check` + POST /api/v1/health-doctor/run.

 -- Gerald KERMA <devel@cybermind.fr>  Tue, 19 May 2026 08:00:00 +0200
